config HCP_BENCH
	bool "Bench / HIL firmware: bring-up aids on, provisioning off"
	default n
	help
	  A build meant to be run on the test bench rather than shipped: the LED colour
	  cycle and the periodic Modbus poll are compiled in, and hcp::provision is
	  expected to be off so this image also owns the button, the strip and an
	  always-advertising BLE.

	  The raw UART loopback self-test is deliberately NOT part of it: it talks on
	  the same uart1 the Modbus poll uses, so the two would fight for the port.
	  Enable it on its own (-DCONFIG_HCP_SERIAL_LOOPBACK_TEST=y) when you are
	  checking wiring, with the poll off.

	  It is a separate image on purpose - the product build compiles none of that
	  out, and the boot banner says which one is running. Build it with
	  ./build.sh <board> --bench.

config APP_VERSION
	string "firmware version (dotted numeric: major.minor.patch)"
	default "0.1.0"
	help
	  The one version knob of a build. Reported on the <sn>/online topic and used
	  by hcp::ota as "what am I running", so an update is only taken when the
	  server offers something above it. MCUboot compares the version in the image
	  header (CONFIG_MCUBOOT_IMGTOOL_SIGN_VERSION), not this string, so the two
	  have to move together: ./build.sh <board> --version <x.y.z> sets both.

source "Kconfig.zephyr"
